C/ Verifies TASN (whole-structure assign, `DST = SRC;`) correctly deep-
C/ copies a structure with a VECTOR terminal -- previously aborted
C/ entirely the moment it reached the first ARRAY/MATRIX/VECTOR
C/ terminal (UTIL_PARM's own V VECTOR is declared *first*, so before
C/ this fix TASN would have failed before copying even the later
C/ scalar/integer/BOOLEAN fields). SRC is READ once, copied to DST, then
C/ SRC's own scalar fields are overwritten by a second READ -- DST's own
C/ fields still holding the *first* READ's values proves TASN performed
C/ a genuine independent copy, not an aliased reference (displaying the
C/ VECTOR terminal's own copied value isn't possible yet -- a separate,
C/ pre-existing gap -- so this checks every other terminal instead).

  TTASNARR: PROGRAM;
     STRUCTURE UTIL_PARM:
        1 V VECTOR,
        1 S1 SCALAR,
        1 C INTEGER,
        1 S2 SCALAR,
        1 E BOOLEAN;
     DECLARE SRC UTIL_PARM-STRUCTURE;
     DECLARE DST UTIL_PARM-STRUCTURE;

     READ(5) SRC;
     DST = SRC;
     READ(5) SRC;
     WRITE(6) DST.S1, DST.C, DST.S2, DST.E;
Y %SVCI(0);
  CLOSE TTASNARR;
